<link rel="stylesheet" href="/s-18v2lq.css"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://nclexsim.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Care coordination","item":"https://nclexsim.com/nursing-care-coordination"}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebPage","name":"Nursing Care Coordination: The RN's Real Job","description":"Care coordination is the RN's real job and the NCLEX-RN's biggest category: Management of Care. Vexcura trains it, from single-patient drills to a Shift sim.","url":"https://nclexsim.com/nursing-care-coordination","inLanguage":"en-US","isPartOf":{"@type":"WebSite","name":"Vexcura","url":"https://nclexsim.com/"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://nclexsim.com/#org"},"about":[{"@type":"Thing","name":"Care coordination"},{"@type":"Thing","name":"NCLEX-RN Management of Care"},{"@type":"Thing","name":"Nursing delegation and prioritization"},{"@type":"Thing","name":"Nursing clinical judgment"}],"audience":{"@type":"EducationalAudience","educationalRole":"teacher","audienceType":"Nursing schools, nursing faculty and nursing students"}}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"SoftwareApplication","name":"Vexcura care coordination training","description":"Nursing care coordination practice for the NCLEX-RN Management of Care category: single-patient clinical judgment drills up to a multi-patient Shift simulation with a live delegation engine, assignment, interdisciplinary coordination, transitions of care and a scored debrief by competency.","url":"https://nclexsim.com/nursing-care-coordination","applicationCategory":"EducationalApplication","applicationSubCategory":"Nursing education","operatingSystem":"Any (web browser)","featureList":["Multi-patient Shift simulation capstone","Charge-nurse assignment of several patients","Prioritization across a full assignment","Live delegation engine using the Five Rights and RN, LPN and UAP scope","Interdisciplinary coordination in Secure Chat","Transitions of care: report, handoff and discharge","Scored debrief by competency","Adaptive single-patient deteriorating-patient drill","Maps to every Management of Care sub-skill"],"audience":{"@type":"EducationalAudience","educationalRole":"teacher","audienceType":"Nursing schools, nursing faculty and clinical instructors"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://nclexsim.com/#org"}}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is care coordination in nursing?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Care coordination is the registered nurse's work of organizing a patient's care across people and time: setting priorities, delegating and assigning tasks within each team member's scope, advocating for the patient, collaborating with the provider, pharmacy and therapies, managing referrals and resources, and handing the patient off so nothing is lost between shifts or units. On the NCLEX-RN it is the Management of Care category."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Management of Care the biggest category on the NCLEX-RN?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. In the 2026 NCLEX-RN Test Plan, Management of Care makes up 15% to 21% of the exam\u003csup>\u003ca href=\"#ccsrc-ncsbn-testplan\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">1\u003c/a>\u003c/sup>, the largest single share of any client needs category. It sits under Safe and Effective Care Environment and covers prioritization, delegation, assignment, advocacy, continuity of care, collaboration, referrals, and legal and ethical rights."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do you practice delegation for the NCLEX?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Practice it as a decision, not a definition. Vexcura's Shift simulation gives you several patients and a team of an LPN and a UAP, and asks you to hand off each task. A live delegation engine checks your choice against the Five Rights of delegation and each role's scope of practice, drawn from the 2019 NCSBN and ANA national delegation guidelines, and the debrief explains every call. The free NCLEX delegation questions on this site drill the same reasoning in question form."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does the Shift simulation do?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Shift simulation is Vexcura's multi-patient capstone. You take report on an assignment of several patients, build your plan for the shift, and then prioritize across them as new cues arrive. You delegate and assign tasks to a simulated LPN and UAP within scope, coordinate with the provider, pharmacy and other disciplines in Secure Chat, manage transitions of care, and give an end-of-shift handoff. A scored debrief grades you by competency: prioritization, delegation, assignment, advocacy, continuity and collaboration."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does it cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Students and instructors are always free; the school or facility pays for the license. Every plan includes every feature, including the Shift simulation and the single-patient drills, per year: Per student $199 per student seat; Site 100 $15,000; Site 250 $30,000; Site 500 $50,000; Custom Custom quote. Founding programs: 50% off the first paid year. A free one-semester pilot covers one clinical group or cohort, with no obligation to buy."}}]}</script></head><body><header class="top"><div class="w"><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Vexcura home"><svg class="vxw" viewBox="-2 -86 472 96" aria-hidden="true"><style>@property --vxa{syntax:"<color>";inherits:true;initial-value:#4b4f86}@property --vxb{syntax:"<color>";inherits:true;initial-value:#d77a6a}@property --vxc{syntax:"<color>";inherits:true;initial-value:#f8c27a}@property --vxrb{syntax:"<color>";inherits:true;initial-value:#f8c27a}@property --vxrc{