    <p class="mh">Account</p><a class="mt" href="/#signup"><b>Join with a school code</b><small>Or request access</small></a><a class="mt" href="/#signin"><b>Sign in</b><small>Already have one</small></a>
   </div></details></nav></div></header><script>(function(){var d=document.querySelector(".mnav");if(!d)return;document.addEventListener("click",function(e){if(d.open&&!d.contains(e.target))d.open=false});document.addEventListener("keydown",function(e){if(e.key==="Escape"&&d.open){d.open=false;d.querySelector("summary").focus()}})})();</script><main><nav class="crumb w" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › <span>Care coordination</span></nav><section class="hero w hv"><div><h1>Nursing Care Coordination: The RN's Real Job</h1><p class="lead">Most NCLEX prep drills what nurses know. The registered nurse's actual work is coordinating care: prioritizing, delegating, advocating and handing off safely. That is also the NCLEX-RN's largest category, Management of Care. Vexcura is built to train it.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="#the-shift">See the Shift simulation</a><a class="btn alt" href="/for-nursing-schools#pilot">Request a pilot</a></div></div><figure class="shot duo"><div class="duo-s"><div class="dv dv-b"><div class="dv-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span><svg viewBox="0 0 12 14" width="9" height="11" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6V4.2a3 3 0 0 1 6 0V6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><rect x="1.5" y="6" width="9" height="7" rx="1.6" fill="currentColor"/></svg>nclexsim.com</span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/shift-board-1000.webp" srcset="/img/shift-board-1600.webp 1600w, /img/shift-board-1000.webp 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 860px) calc(100vw - 72px), 560px" width="1000" height="625" alt="The Shift simulation assignment board: six demo patients with rooms, vital signs, acuity and a see-first order, an in-basket of events, and delegate controls" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div></div><div class="dv dv-p dv-po" style="--sb:#1a4e71"><div class="dv-s"><div class="dv-sb lt" aria-hidden="true"><time class="vx-now" data-f="sb"></time><span class="dv-isl"></span><span class="dv-ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 18 12" width="17" height="11"><rect x="0" y="8" width="3" height="4" rx=".8"/><rect x="5" y="5.5" width="3" height="6.5" rx=".8"/><rect x="10" y="3" width="3" height="9" rx=".8"/><rect x="15" y="0" width="3" height="12" rx=".8"/></svg><svg viewBox="0 0 16 12" width="15" height="11"><path d="M8 11.6 5.6 9.2a3.4 3.4 0 0 1 4.8 0z"/><path d="M3.4 7A6.5 6.5 0 0 1 12.6 7l-1.3 1.3a4.7 4.7 0 0 0-6.6 0z"/><path d="M1.1 4.7a9.7 9.7 0 0 1 13.8 0l-1.3 1.3a7.9 7.9 0 0 0-11.2 0z"/></svg><svg viewBox="0 0 27 13" width="25" height="12"><rect x=".6" y=".6" width="22.8" height="11.8" rx="3.4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity=".4" stroke-width="1.2"/><rect x="2.4" y="2.4" width="17.6" height="8.2" rx="2"/><path d="M25 4.4v4.2c.9-.3 1.4-1.1 1.4-2.1s-.5-1.8-1.4-2.1z" fill-opacity=".45"/></svg></span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/dx-phone-780.webp" srcset="/img/dx-phone-400.webp 400w, /img/dx-phone-780.webp 780w" sizes="(max-width: 860px) 30vw, 160px" width="780" height="1600" alt="A drill on a phone: the nursing assistant reports new slurred speech and facial droop on a made-up patient, with Assess, Act and Call tabs" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div></div></div></div><figcaption>A nurse coordinating a full patient assignment, on a laptop and a phone. Demo data.</figcaption></figure></section><div class="w"><nav aria-label="On this page"><ul><li><a href="#real-job">Care coordination is the RN's real job</a></li><li><a href="#management-of-care">Management of Care: the biggest NCLEX-RN category</a></li><li><a href="#ladder">The capability ladder</a></li><li><a href="#the-shift">The Shift simulation</a></li><li><a href="#subskills">Every sub-skill, and where you practice it</a></li></ul></nav><section id="real-job"><h2>Care coordination is the RN's real job</h2><p>Nursing programs spend most of their time teaching what nurses <em>know</em>: labs, medications, diseases. That knowledge matters, but it is not the job. The registered nurse's job is to <b>coordinate care</b>, to take a group of patients and a team of people and keep everything moving safely: deciding what to do first, handing the right task to the right person, speaking up for the patient, pulling in the provider and pharmacy and therapies, and handing off cleanly at the end of the shift.</p><p>Vexcura is built around that work. The single-patient simulations train the judgment a nurse brings to one patient; the <a href="#the-shift">Shift simulation</a> puts that judgment to work across a whole assignment, which is where coordination actually happens.</p></section><section id="management-of-care"><h2>Management of Care: the biggest category on the NCLEX-RN</h2><p>Care coordination is not a side topic on the licensure exam. In the 2026 NCLEX-RN Test Plan it is the <b>Management of Care</b> category, 15% to 21% of the exam<sup><a href="#ccsrc-ncsbn-testplan" aria-label="Source 1">1</a></sup>, the largest single share of any client needs category. It falls under Safe and Effective Care Environment, and the test plan lists its sub-skills explicitly: establishing priorities, delegation, assignment, advocacy, continuity of care, collaboration with the interdisciplinary team, referrals, and the client's legal and ethical rights.</p><p>The Next Generation NCLEX raised the stakes by measuring clinical judgment directly, through the <a href="/next-generation-nclex">NCSBN Clinical Judgment Measurement Model</a><sup><a href="#ccsrc-ncsbn-cjmm" aria-label="Source 3">3</a></sup>: recognizing cues, analyzing them, prioritizing, generating solutions, taking action and evaluating outcomes. Prioritization and the decision of who acts are coordination skills, and they are exactly what an unfolding case study asks you to do.</p></section><section id="ladder"><h2>The capability ladder: from one patient to a full shift</h2><p>You cannot coordinate a team of people on a floor of patients until you can read one patient well. Vexcura builds coordination in two rungs, and every rung is included in every plan.</p><h3>Rung one: single-patient clinical judgment</h3><p class="soon" style="background:var(--good-soft)"><b style="color:var(--good)">Available now</b> In every plan</p><p>Everything a nurse does for a whole assignment starts with one patient who is changing. These simulations, all inside the <a href="/academic-ehr-for-nursing-students">Epic-style academic EHR</a>, train that judgment:</p>
         <ul><li><b><a href="/nursing-simulation-scenarios#deteriorating-patient">The adaptive deteriorating-patient drill</a>:</b> 59 hidden cases in 4 tiers up to the ICU and emergency department. The patient's physiology responds to what the student does, and the student calls a simulated provider with SBAR.</li>
         <li><b><a href="/nursing-simulation-scenarios#telemetry">Telemetry and EKG</a>:</b> 53 computer-generated rhythms with calipers, a central station and alarms.</li>
         <li><b><a href="/nursing-simulation-scenarios#auscultation">Assessment and Auscultation</a>:</b> a virtual stethoscope over a body map, and a full head-to-toe assessment charted on the flowsheet.</li>
         <li><b>The academic EHR itself:</b> My Chart, the MAR, spreadsheet-style flowsheets, orders, the LDA avatar, SDOH screening and Secure Chat, on made-up patients.</li></ul>
         <figure class="shot"><div class="dv dv-b"><div class="dv-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span><svg viewBox="0 0 12 14" width="9" height="11" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6V4.2a3 3 0 0 1 6 0V6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><rect x="1.5" y="6" width="9" height="7" rx="1.6" fill="currentColor"/></svg>nclexsim.com</span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/dx-run-1000.webp" srcset="/img/dx-run-1440.webp 1440w, /img/dx-run-1000.webp 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 32px), 720px" width="1000" height="625" alt="A deteriorating-patient drill starting on a made-up practice patient: the drill panel with a call light, handoff, a respiratory assessment filed to flowsheets, and Assess, Act and Call actions" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div></div><figcaption>A single-patient deteriorating drill in the academic EHR. Made-up patient.</figcaption></figure>
         <p>See the single-patient work in full on <a href="/nursing-simulation-scenarios">nursing simulation scenarios and drills</a> and <a href="/virtual-nursing-simulation">virtual nursing simulation</a>.</p><h3>Rung two: coordinate a full assignment</h3><p class="soon" style="background:var(--good-soft)"><b style="color:var(--good)">Available now</b> In every plan</p><p>The capstone is the <a href="#the-shift">Shift simulation</a>, below: several patients at once, a team to delegate to, and a scored debrief of how well the student coordinated it all.</p></section><section id="the-shift"><h2>The Shift simulation: coordinate a full patient load</h2><p class="soon" style="background:var(--good-soft)"><b style="color:var(--good)">Available now</b> In every plan</p><p>The Shift simulation is Vexcura's multi-patient capstone. Instead of one deteriorating patient, the student takes a charge-style assignment of several patients and has to keep the whole floor safe for a shift, the way a working nurse does.</p>
         <figure class="shot"><div class="dv dv-b"><div class="dv-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span><svg viewBox="0 0 12 14" width="9" height="11" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6V4.2a3 3 0 0 1 6 0V6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><rect x="1.5" y="6" width="9" height="7" rx="1.6" fill="currentColor"/></svg>nclexsim.com</span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/shift-board-1000.webp" srcset="/img/shift-board-1600.webp 1600w, /img/shift-board-1000.webp 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 32px), 720px" width="1000" height="625" alt="The Shift simulation assignment board: six demo patients with rooms, vital signs, acuity and a see-first order, an in-basket of events, and delegate controls" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div></div><figcaption>The Shift assignment board: several patients, their tasks and the team. Demo data.</figcaption></figure>
         <h3>Take report and build the plan</h3><p>The shift opens with handoff on every patient. The student takes report, sets up a plan for the shift, and sees the worklist fill with what each patient needs and when.</p>
         <figure class="shot"><div class="dv dv-b"><div class="dv-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span><svg viewBox="0 0 12 14" width="9" height="11" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6V4.2a3 3 0 0 1 6 0V6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><rect x="1.5" y="6" width="9" height="7" rx="1.6" fill="currentColor"/></svg>nclexsim.com</span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/shift-assign-1000.webp" srcset="/img/shift-assign-1600.webp 1600w, /img/shift-assign-1000.webp 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 32px), 720px" width="1000" height="625" alt="Taking report at the start of a shift in Vexcura: handoff cards for each patient before the shift begins" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div></div><figcaption>Starting a shift: the assignment and the plan for the day. Fictional patients.</figcaption></figure>
         <h3>Prioritize across patients</h3><p>Cues arrive from several rooms at once: a monitor alarm, a call light, a lab that just resulted, a family question. The student has to decide which patient to see first and which task can wait, and the simulation records the order and the timing.</p>
         <div class="split"><div class="st"><h3>Delegate and assign, within scope</h3><p>The student works with a team, typically an LPN and a UAP, and hands off tasks and whole patients. A <b>live delegation engine</b> checks every choice against the <b>Five Rights of delegation</b> (right task, right circumstance, right person, right directions and communication, and right supervision and evaluation) and against each role's scope of practice, drawn from the 2019 NCSBN and ANA national delegation guidelines<sup><a href="#ccsrc-ncsbn-ana-delegation" aria-label="Source 2">2</a></sup>. Delegate a sterile dressing change or patient teaching to a UAP and the engine stops you and explains why; assign an unstable patient to the LPN and it flags the assignment.</p></div><figure class="shot"><div class="dv dv-b"><div class="dv-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span><svg viewBox="0 0 12 14" width="9" height="11" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6V4.2a3 3 0 0 1 6 0V6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><rect x="1.5" y="6" width="9" height="7" rx="1.6" fill="currentColor"/></svg>nclexsim.com</span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/shift-delegate-1000.webp" srcset="/img/shift-delegate-1600.webp 1600w, /img/shift-delegate-1000.webp 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 32px), 720px" width="1000" height="625" alt="Prioritizing across a full patient assignment in the Shift simulation, deciding who to see first and what to delegate within scope" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div></div><figcaption>The delegation engine checks a task against the Five Rights and the delegatee's scope. Demo data.</figcaption></figure></div>
         <h3>Coordinate the interdisciplinary team</h3><p>The student pulls in the rest of the team the way a nurse does: paging the provider with SBAR, messaging pharmacy about a dose, and requesting physical therapy or social work, all in Secure Chat with a simulated care team.</p>
         <h3>Manage transitions of care</h3><p>Care coordination is mostly about handoffs. The Shift simulation runs report at the start, an end-of-shift handoff at the end, and transfers and discharges in between, so the student practices moving a patient between people and settings without losing information, the heart of continuity of care.</p>
         <div class="split rev"><div class="st"><h3>A scored debrief, by competency</h3><p>When the shift ends, the debrief grades the student by coordination competency: how they prioritized across patients, whether each delegation and assignment was appropriate, how they advocated, how they collaborated, and how clean their handoffs were. Every call is explained with its source, the same way the single-patient drill debrief works.</p></div><figure class="shot"><div class="dv dv-b"><div class="dv-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span><svg viewBox="0 0 12 14" width="9" height="11" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6V4.2a3 3 0 0 1 6 0V6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><rect x="1.5" y="6" width="9" height="7" rx="1.6" fill="currentColor"/></svg>nclexsim.com</span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/shift-debrief-1000.webp" srcset="/img/shift-debrief-1600.webp 1600w, /img/shift-debrief-1000.webp 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 32px), 720px" width="1000" height="625" alt="The scored Shift debrief: a shift score with Management of Care competency bars for prioritization, delegation, patient safety and continuity of care" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div></div><figcaption>A Shift debrief: the shift timeline and the score by coordination competency. Demo student.</figcaption></figure></div>
         <p class="src" style="color:var(--muted);font-size:14.5px">All patients and teammates are fictional. The delegation engine and scoring are rule-based; optional AI only rewords replies and is labeled in the app. A debrief score is practice feedback, not a prediction of an NCLEX result. Confirm scope-of-practice rules against your state's nurse practice act and your facility's policies.</p></section><section id="subskills"><h2>Every Management of Care sub-skill, and where you practice it</h2><p>The NCLEX-RN Test Plan names the Management of Care sub-skills. Here is each one, in plain terms, and where a student practices it in Vexcura.</p>
         <div class="tw"><table><thead><tr><th>Sub-skill</th><th>What it means</th><th>Where you practice it</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>Establishing priorities</b></td><td>Decide which patient the RN sees first and which problem to act on first.</td><td>The deteriorating-patient drill and the Shift simulation, plus <a href="/nclex-prioritization-questions">NCLEX prioritization questions</a>.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Delegation</b></td><td>Match each task to the right team member and follow the Five Rights of delegation.</td><td>The Shift simulation's delegation engine, plus <a href="/nclex-delegation-questions">NCLEX delegation questions</a>.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Assignment of care</b></td><td>Give a whole patient to the right RN, LPN or UAP for the shift, within scope.</td><td>The Shift simulation: the charge-nurse assignment board.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Advocacy</b></td><td>Speak for the patient: informed consent, the right to refuse, and questioning an unsafe order.</td><td>Secure Chat and SBAR calls in the academic EHR, where the student can hold or question an order.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Continuity of care</b></td><td>Hand the patient off, between shifts and between units, without losing information.</td><td>SBAR handoff and the printable chart report in the academic EHR, and the Shift simulation's end-of-shift report.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Collaboration with the interdisciplinary team</b></td><td>Work with the provider, pharmacy, physical therapy and social work toward one plan.</td><td>Secure Chat with a simulated care team, used in drills and in the Shift simulation.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Referrals and resource management</b></td><td>Connect the patient to the services they need after discharge.</td><td>SDOH screening with community resources in the <a href="/academic-ehr-for-nursing-students">academic EHR</a>.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Legal and ethical rights</b></td><td>Informed consent, advance directives, confidentiality (HIPAA) and incident reporting.</td><td>The <a href="/nclex-practice-questions/management-of-care">Management of Care question bank</a>, with cited rationales.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><h2 id="pricing">Included in every plan</h2><p>Care coordination practice, from the single-patient drills to the Shift simulation, is included in every Vexcura plan, and students and instructors never pay. Plans differ only in how many students they cover, per year: Per student $199 per student seat · Site 100 $15,000 · Site 250 $30,000 · Site 500 $50,000 · Custom: Custom quote. Founding programs: 50% off the first paid year. A free one-semester pilot covers one clinical group or cohort, with no obligation to buy. <a href="/for-nursing-schools#pricing">Pricing for schools</a></p><h2>Common questions</h2><details class="faq"><summary>What is care coordination in nursing?</summary><p>Care coordination is the registered nurse's work of organizing a patient's care across people and time: setting priorities, delegating and assigning tasks within each team member's scope, advocating for the patient, collaborating with the provider, pharmacy and therapies, managing referrals and resources, and handing the patient off so nothing is lost between shifts or units. On the NCLEX-RN it is the Management of Care category.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Is Management of Care the biggest category on the NCLEX-RN?</summary><p>Yes. In the 2026 NCLEX-RN Test Plan, Management of Care makes up 15% to 21% of the exam&lt;sup&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#ccsrc-ncsbn-testplan&quot; aria-label=&quot;Source 1&quot;&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;, the largest single share of any client needs category. It sits under Safe and Effective Care Environment and covers prioritization, delegation, assignment, advocacy, continuity of care, collaboration, referrals, and legal and ethical rights.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>How do you practice delegation for the NCLEX?</summary><p>Practice it as a decision, not a definition. Vexcura's Shift simulation gives you several patients and a team of an LPN and a UAP, and asks you to hand off each task. A live delegation engine checks your choice against the Five Rights of delegation and each role's scope of practice, drawn from the 2019 NCSBN and ANA national delegation guidelines, and the debrief explains every call. The free NCLEX delegation questions on this site drill the same reasoning in question form.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>What does the Shift simulation do?</summary><p>The Shift simulation is Vexcura's multi-patient capstone. You take report on an assignment of several patients, build your plan for the shift, and then prioritize across them as new cues arrive. You delegate and assign tasks to a simulated LPN and UAP within scope, coordinate with the provider, pharmacy and other disciplines in Secure Chat, manage transitions of care, and give an end-of-shift handoff. A scored debrief grades you by competency: prioritization, delegation, assignment, advocacy, continuity and collaboration.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>How much does it cost?</summary><p>Students and instructors are always free; the school or facility pays for the license. Every plan includes every feature, including the Shift simulation and the single-patient drills, per year: Per student $199 per student seat; Site 100 $15,000; Site 250 $30,000; Site 500 $50,000; Custom Custom quote. Founding programs: 50% off the first paid year. A free one-semester pilot covers one clinical group or cohort, with no obligation to buy. <a href="/for-nursing-schools#pricing">See pricing</a>.</p></details><h2 id="sources">Sources</h2><ol class="src"><li id="ccsrc-ncsbn-testplan">National Council of State Boards of Nursing. 2026 NCLEX-RN Test Plan. Chicago, IL: NCSBN; effective April 2026. Management of Care is 15% to 21% of the NCLEX-RN. <a href="https://www.ncsbn.org/exams/testplans.page" rel="noopener">ncsbn.org</a></li><li id="ccsrc-ncsbn-ana-delegation">National Council of State Boards of Nursing and American Nurses Association. National Guidelines for Nursing Delegation (ANA, NCSBN joint statement). 2019. <a href="https://www.nursingworld.org/~4962ca/globalassets/practiceandpolicy/nursing-excellence/ana-position-statements/nursing-practice/ana-ncsbn-joint-statement-on-delegation.pdf" rel="noopener">nursingworld.org</a></li><li id="ccsrc-ncsbn-cjmm">National Council of State Boards of Nursing. NCLEX-RN Clinical Judgment Measurement Model (NCJMM). 2019. <a href="https://www.ncsbn.org/14798.htm" rel="noopener">ncsbn.org</a></li></ol><p class="src">NCLEX-RN® and Next Generation NCLEX® are registered trademarks of the National Council of State Boards of Nursing, Inc. (NCSBN). Vexcura is independent and isn't affiliated with or endorsed by NCSBN, the American Nurses Association or any board of nursing. Epic is a trademark of Epic Systems Corporation; "Epic-style" describes a familiar layout. All patients are fictional.</p><h2>More for nursing programs</h2><ul class="rel"><li><a href="/for-nursing-schools">Vexcura for nursing schools</a></li><li><a href="/clinical-instructor-tools">Clinical instructor tools</a></li><li><a href="/academic-ehr-for-nursing-students">Academic EHR for nursing students</a></li><li><a href="/nursing-simulation-scenarios">Nursing simulation scenarios and drills</a></li><li><a href="/nursing-board-compliance">Board of nursing compliance (GA, TN, AL)</a></li><li><a href="/virtual-nursing-simulation">Virtual nursing simulation (VR coming soon)</a></li><li><a href="/nursing-lms-integration">Canvas, Blackboard, D2L and Moodle integration</a></li></ul><h2>Related</h2><ul class="rel"><li><a href="/nursing-simulation-scenarios">Nursing simulation scenarios and drills</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-prioritization-questions">NCLEX prioritization questions</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-delegation-questions">NCLEX delegation questions</a></li><li><a href="/for-nursing-schools">Vexcura for nursing schools</a></li><li><a href="/academic-ehr-for-nursing-students">Epic-style academic EHR</a></li></ul></div><section class="band vxs-band"><div class="vxs-bg" data-vxs-i="0" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="vxs-sh" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="w"><h2>Try Vexcura with one cohort for a semester, free</h2><p>Pick one clinical group or course. Faculty accounts are always free. At the end of the semester you decide whether to license it for your program; there's no obligation to buy, and every plan includes everything. Founding programs: 50% off the first paid year.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/for-nursing-schools#pilot">Request a pilot</a><a class="btn alt" href="/for-nursing-schools">How licensing works</a></div></div></section></main><footer class="foot mktf"><div class="w">
